  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad$ Let $a=b-d$ and $c=b+d$, then $a+b+c=21$ $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{b}=7$\r\n\r\nSo, the equation is $\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{c}=14$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ No. of solution $=$ coeff. of $x^{14}$ in $\\left(x+x^{2}+\\ldots .\\right)$ $={ }^{13} \\mathrm{C}_{12}=13$",
